      "message": "Could we keep `unformat_rdma_create_if_args()` independent of the API version?\n\n`allow_port_num` is only needed for legacy VAT compatibility, but it adds version-specific behavior to the shared CLI parser. Let the parser always recognize `port-num`, then have the legacy VAT handlers (`rdma_create` through `rdma_create_v4`) reject a nonzero `args.port_num` after parsing, since those messages cannot serialize it. The CLI and `rdma_create_v5` can use the parsed value directly.",
